Here's a React component that renders a user profile card with name, avatar image, and bio using JSX:

```jsx
import React from 'react';

const UserProfileCard = ({ name, avatarUrl, bio }) => {
  return (
    <div className="user-profile-card">
      <style>{`
        .user-profile-card {
          max-width: 300px;
          margin: 20px auto;
          padding: 20px;
          border-radius: 10px;
          background-color: #f9f9f9;
          box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
          text-align: center;
        }
        .avatar {
          width: 100px;
          height: 100px;
          border-radius: 50%;
          object-fit: cover;
          margin-bottom: 15px;
          border: 2px solid #ddd;
        }
        .name {
          font-size: 1.5rem;
          font-weight: bold;
          margin-bottom: 10px;
          color: #333;
        }
        .bio {
          font-size: 1rem;
          color: #666;
          line-height: 1.5;
        }
      `}</style>

      <img src={avatarUrl} alt={name} className="avatar" />
      <h3 className="name">{name}</h3>
      <p className="bio">{bio}</p>
    </div>
  );
};

export default UserProfileCard;
```

This component:

1. Accepts three props: `name`, `avatarUrl`, and `bio`
2. Uses a functional component with an inline style block for CSS
3. Renders an avatar image with appropriate styling
4. Displays the user's name in a heading
5. Shows the bio in a paragraph
6. Includes basic responsive styling with a centered layout

You can use this component like:

```jsx
<UserProfileCard 
  name="Jane Doe" 
  avatarUrl="https://example.com/jane-doe.jpg" 
  bio="Software developer, coffee enthusiast, and travel lover." 
/>
```

